5.5 STREAM‑RNN and Differentiable Spectral‑Norm Stability

For recurrent extensions, we add an optical feedback delay line and enforce stability via a differentiable penalty on the spectral norm of the recurrent weight matrix, computed on‑chip using power iteration. This avoids hard projections and integrates with AVM.

5.6 Programming Model and Compiler Support

We propose a software stack (Figure 5.6) consisting of:

· Frontend: PyTorch/ONNX graph. An operator‑splitting pass identifies consecutive ReLU layer pairs and fuses them into STREAM layers.
· Placement & routing: A tool maps the logical SVD parameters to physical MZI locations, exploiting butterfly sparsity and fault maps.
· Runtime calibration: At power‑up, the fault‑mapping protocol is executed; a closed‑loop controller maintains LO phase lock.
  This compiler‑directed approach is critical for bridging the gap between algorithm and hardware, an area identified as underexplored in recent patent landscapes.

