7. Experimental Validation Strategy and Risk Mitigation

We outline a three‑phase tape‑out roadmap to validate STREAM‑PNN experimentally.

Phase 1 (4×4 proof‑of‑concept): Target IMEC iSiPP50G multiproject wafer. Validate the operator‑splitting activation and AVM gradient on a small mesh. Key risk: PCM integration may exceed back‑end voltage limits; mitigation: use external bond pads for programming.

Phase 2 (16×16 with hybrid PCM): AIM Photonics 300 nm process. Demonstrate fault‑tolerant mesh, hybrid weight storage, and WDM operation with 4 wavelengths. Monte Carlo yield analysis (Figure 7.1) shows >95% yield at 1% defect rate using three‑splitter MZIs and redundancy.

Phase 3 (32×32 full system): Tower 45 nm with integrated Ge‑APDs. Full STREAM‑PNN with 5 layers, balanced detection, and compiler integration. Target MNIST/CIFAR‑10 classification accuracy within 1% of software baseline.

A risk register (Table 7.2) identifies the top risks: laser coupling efficiency, thermal crosstalk, PCM voltage limits, and ADC power. Each risk includes a mitigation strategy and fallback option.

