A.1 Proof of Theorem 2.1 (Phase‑Angle Equivalence)

Theorem 2.1. Let \mathbf{W} = \mathbf{U} \boldsymbol{\Sigma} \mathbf{V}^\dagger be the SVD of a weight matrix. There exists a bijection between the N(N-1) phase shifter angles \{\phi_{ij}^U, \phi_{ij}^V\} of the MZI meshes implementing \mathbf{U} and \mathbf{V} and the entries of \mathbf{U}, \mathbf{V}. Consequently, the electronic weight \mathbf{W} and the optical parameter set (\{\phi_{ij}^U\},\{\sigma_i\},\{\phi_{ij}^V\}) contain identical information.

Proof. The Reck–Zeilinger decomposition expresses any unitary matrix \mathbf{U} \in U(N) as a product of L = N(N-1)/2 two‑dimensional unitary rotations T_{ij}(\theta_{ij},\phi_{ij}), each implemented by a single MZI. The nulling procedure proceeds column by column from left to right and, within each column, from bottom to top. At step (i,j) with i>j, we consider the (i,j) entry of the partially processed matrix \mathbf{U}^{(j)}. The rotation

T_{ij}(\theta,\phi) = \begin{pmatrix} \sin\theta\, e^{i\phi} & \cos\theta \\ \cos\theta & -\sin\theta\, e^{i\phi} \end{pmatrix},

acting on rows j and i, is chosen so that the new (i,j) entry vanishes:

\cos\theta \cdot U^{(j)}_{jj} - \sin\theta\, e^{i\phi} \cdot U^{(j)}_{ij} = 0.

Solving this determines \phi_{ij} and \theta_{ij} uniquely, up to a global phase ambiguity that does not affect the resulting unitary. Explicitly,

\phi_{ij} = \arg\left(\frac{U^{(j)}_{jj}}{U^{(j)}_{ij}}\right), \qquad
\theta_{ij} = \arctan\!\left(\frac{|U^{(j)}_{jj}|}{|U^{(j)}_{ij}|}\right).

Because the nulling sequence is deterministic—the choice of which entry to zero at each step is fixed by the triangular layout—the mapping from the matrix entries to the set of N(N-1) phase angles is a well‑defined function. Conversely, given the full set of angles, the matrix \mathbf{U} is uniquely reconstructed as the product of the corresponding inverse rotations in reverse order. The nulling steps are reversible: each step is a unitary transformation that can be inverted. Therefore the mapping is bijective onto the subset of U(N) reachable by the mesh, which is all of U(N) for the triangular layout. An identical construction holds for \mathbf{V}^\dagger. The singular values \{\sigma_i\} are independently set in Tier 3 via attenuators. Hence the combined parameter set (\{\phi_{ij}^U\},\{\sigma_i\},\{\phi_{ij}^V\}) is in one‑to‑one correspondence with the weight matrix \mathbf{W}. ∎

