A.4 Error Propagation in Non‑Ideal MZI Meshes

A physical MZI with target splitting angle \theta implements the 2\times 2 unitary

T(\theta,\phi) = i \begin{pmatrix} \sin\theta\, e^{i\phi} & \cos\theta \\ \cos\theta & -\sin\theta\, e^{i\phi} \end{pmatrix}.

Manufacturing imperfections introduce static errors \delta\theta_\ell per MZI \ell. Expanding the implemented unitary \mathbf{U}_{\text{actual}} = \prod_{\ell=1}^L T_\ell(\theta_\ell + \delta\theta_\ell, \phi_\ell) to first order yields

\mathbf{U}_{\text{actual}} = \mathbf{U}_{\text{ideal}} + \sum_{\ell=1}^L \frac{\partial \mathbf{U}_{\text{ideal}}}{\partial \theta_\ell} \delta\theta_\ell + O(\delta\theta^2).

The error matrix \Delta\mathbf{U} = \sum_\ell \mathbf{J}_\ell \delta\theta_\ell with \mathbf{J}_\ell = \partial \mathbf{U}_{\text{ideal}} / \partial \theta_\ell. The Frobenius norm squared is

\|\Delta\mathbf{U}\|_F^2 = \sum_{\ell,\ell'} \operatorname{tr}(\mathbf{J}_\ell^\dagger \mathbf{J}_{\ell'}) \delta\theta_\ell \delta\theta_{\ell'}.

Taking the expectation over the Gaussian fabrication error with covariance \boldsymbol{\Sigma}_\theta gives

\mathbb{E}\!\left[\|\Delta\mathbf{U}\|_F^2\right] = \operatorname{tr}\!\left( \mathbf{J}^\top \boldsymbol{\Sigma}_\theta \mathbf{J} \right) \le 4 \operatorname{tr}(\boldsymbol{\Sigma}_\theta) \le 2 N^2 \bar{\sigma}_\theta^2,

since \|\mathbf{J}_\ell\|_F \le 2. For the three‑splitter MZI, the sensitivity \partial T/\partial \theta is reduced by a factor \gamma < 1, tightening the bound.

